#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087431 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e905212-8796-5742-a83e-892fdf66eced" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing an Expression that Represents the Derivative of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "36199fc1-505f-5179-9eeb-bec0534bab5f" :question/math-academy-id "e-128" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = x^2$, what is $f'(x)$ according to the definition of the derivative?" :question/worked-solution "The derivative $f '(x)$ is given by the limit\n\n$$\n\\lim_{h\\to 0} \\dfrac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\nf(x) = x^2\n$$\n\n, we have that\n\n$$\nf(x+h) = (x+h)^2\n$$\n\nHence, we get\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle f'(x)=\\lim_{h\\to 0} \\dfrac{(x+h)^2-x^2}{h}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087432 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087881 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c6f3c71-d11b-59af-bad6-5f5c0ff6634f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "7fb64010-dc03-5db5-b5d1-563d2fe44b6d" :question/math-academy-id "e-130" :question/problem "Given $y =x^2$, calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ using the limit of a difference quotient." :question/worked-solution "We let $y=f(x)$ and apply the formula for the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= lim_(h → 0)(f(x + h) - f(x))/(h) \\\\\n&= lim_(h → 0)((x + h)^{2} - x^{2})/(h) \\\\\n&= lim_(h → 0)\\frac{x^{2} + 2xh + h^{2} - x^{2}}{h} \\\\\n&= lim_(h → 0)\\frac{2xh + h^{2}}{h} \\\\\n&= lim_(h → 0)(\\frac{2xh}{h} + \\frac{h^{2}}{h}) \\\\\n&= lim_(h → 0)(2x + h) \\\\\n&= 2x + 0 \\\\\n&= 2x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
